: true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-cap30-19-off/omp-19/cells/with/trig-omp-multistep/12/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/12.18.3 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/a95d432f7bc115e3b642c41ee48344d81c6221c7/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "The bug is in `to_cents`: `int(19.99 * 100)` truncates `1998.9999\u2026` to `1998`. Round in decimal space instead of truncating.\nFixed. The bug was in `ledger/currency.py` in `to_cents`: it did `int(amount * 100)`, and `int()` cuts off the fractional part instead of rounding. Floats can't hold most decimal prices exactly, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999\u2026` and became `1998` cents. The same thing happened with `0.29` and `4.35`, which is why the subtotal, quantity and discount tests failed.\n\n**Change:** `to_cents` now converts the amount with `Decimal(str(amount))`, multiplies by 100, and rounds half up to a whole number of cents. Going through `str` keeps the price you meant (`\"19.99\"`) rather than the float's binary approximation. Amounts finer than a cent now round instead of being cut off; this matches the half-up rounding already used in `discounts.py` and `tax.py`.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran every `test_*` function in `tests/test_totals.py` and `tests/test_report.py` directly with `python3`. All 5 passed. I also checked some edge cases: `19.99\u21921999`, `0.29\u219229`, `4.35\u2192435`, `1.005\u2192101`, `-19.99\u2192-1999`, `0\u21920`, `10\u21921000`. To run the suite properly: `pip install pytest && python3 -m pytest tests`.\n\n**Two behaviour changes:**\n- Prices with fractions of a cent now round half up. For negative amounts that means away from zero (\u22121.005 becomes \u2212101). Before, they were silently cut off.\n- If `Line.unit_price` ever comes from user input or a database, passing it as a `Decimal` or string from the start would be cleaner than passing a float. `to_cents` accepts any of these.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 7, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 88530, "requests_cache_write": 23995, "requests_cost_usd": 0.185005, "requests_count": 7, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 2363, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial12", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 23, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:52:08.288778+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 25.265, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2379, "tokens_cache_read": 88530, "tokens_cache_write": 23995, "tokens_fresh": 2379, "tokens_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_cache_read": 88530, "tokens_main_cache_write": 23995, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 2363, "tokens_output": 2363, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 88530, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 23995, "tokens_proxy_calls": 7, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_proxy_output": 2363, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": nu